# Line endings are part of what makes this kit run. Git for Windows checks text out with
# CRLF by default, and bash then dies on the first line of every script ($'\r': command not
# found), and config.sh carries a \r into every value. These rules pin the endings for every
# checkout on every machine. The repo already stores LF, so on a Mac nothing changes.
* text=auto
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.template  text eol=lf
*.plist     text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.md        text eol=lf
